window.docContents[90].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Fs.Select/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Fs___Select":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Fs › Select.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 103 of 134 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nStandard-Descriptor ppoll ProbeModels the Linux AArch64 ppoll syscall (__NR_ppoll = 73, fs/select.c:1109, include/uapi/asm-generic/poll.h:28) restricted to non-blocking descriptor-validity probes on fd ∈ {0, 1, 2} with events = 0, zero timeout, and null signal mask. Any call outside this subset fails closed.\n\n\n\ndef SYS_PPOLLL27–29 ↗#Linux AArch64 ppoll syscall number (__NR_ppoll = 73, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:220, fs/select.c:1109).\n\ndef POLLNVALL31–33 ↗#struct pollfd.revents bit reporting an invalid / closed file descriptor (POLLNVAL = 0x0020, include/uapi/asm-generic/poll.h:19).\n\ndef evalPpollEntriesL35–62 ↗#Evaluate rem 8-byte struct pollfd entries ({ int fd; short events; short revents; }, include/uapi/asm-generic/poll.h:28) starting at index idx from ufds for non-blocking standard-descriptor validity probes (fd ∈ {0, 1, 2}, events = 0):* in Linux do_pollfd (fs/select.c:882), if fdget(fd) finds no open file (fs.fds fd = none), revents receives POLLNVAL (0x0020) and the ready count increments by 1;* if fd is an open .stdio or .localFile descriptor, vfs_poll masked with events | EPOLLERR | EPOLLHUP (events = 0, no error/hangup on regular files or modeled standard streams) yields revents = 0 and leaves the ready count unchanged;* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: any entry outside fd ∈ {0, 1, 2}, with events ≠ 0, or backed by .custom _ returns none so execPpoll fails closed.\n\ndef execPpollL64–132 ↗#ppoll(ufds, nfds, tsp, sigmask, sigsetsize) (__NR_ppoll = 73, SYSCALL_DEFINE5(ppoll) in fs/select.c:1109 and set_user_sigmask in kernel/signal.c:3158), restricted to non-blocking descriptor-validity probes on fd ∈ {0, 1, 2} with events = 0, zero timeout, and null signal mask:* tsp (X2):* tsp == 0 (infinite timeout) fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled ppoll (null timeout)\" ([INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]);* unreadable 16-byte struct __kernel_timespec at tsp returns -EFAULT (get_timespec64);* negative tv_sec, negative tv_nsec, or tv_nsec ≥ 1_000_000_000 returns -EINVAL (poll_select_set_timeout / timespec64_valid in include/linux/time64.h);* any valid non-zero timeout (tv_sec ≠ 0 or tv_nsec ≠ 0) fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled ppoll (non-zero timeout)\";* sigmask (X3) and sigsetsize (X4):* when sigmask == 0, set_user_sigmask (kernel/signal.c:3158) returns 0 immediately without inspecting sigsetsize;* when sigmask ≠ 0 and sigsetsize ≠ 8, returns -EINVAL;* when sigmask ≠ 0 and sigsetsize == 8, fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled ppoll (non-null sigmask)\";* ufds (X0) and nfds (W1, unsigned int nfds in do_sys_poll, fs/select.c:1022):* nfds > FsState.maxOpenFds (fixed ceiling 1024; configurable RLIMIT_NOFILE is not modeled) returns -EINVAL;* nfds == 0 returns 0;* if [ufds, ufds + nfds * 8) wraps modulo 2 ^ 64 or is not readable, returns -EFAULT;* evaluates all nfds entries via evalPpollEntries (failing closed with .Exception \"unmodeled ppoll\" if any entry has fd ∉ {0, 1, 2}, events ≠ 0, or a .custom backend);* if [ufds, ufds + nfds * 8) is not writable (put_user on revents), returns -EFAULT;* otherwise writes revents (0 for open, POLLNVAL for closed) and returns the count of entries with non-zero revents.* [OVERPINNED_BEHAVIOR]: Validates tsp (get_timespec64) -> sigsetsize (set_user_sigmask) -> nfds -> ufds readability/writability, matching fs/select.c:1118-1135.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Fs/Select.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Fs.Select/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Fs___Select"}});